  "objectives": [
    "Determine steric number from a Lewis structure by counting bonding regions and lone pairs around a central atom.",
    "Predict the electron-domain geometry associated with steric numbers 2 through 6 using VSEPR theory.",
    "Distinguish electron-domain geometry from molecular geometry when lone pairs are present.",
    "Explain why lone pairs occupy more angular space than bonding pairs and how this changes bond angles from ideal values.",
    "Apply VSEPR predictions to representative molecules including H2O, NH3, CH4, PF5, SF6, and XeF4."
